# Zapp sibling repository dependency lockfile.
# CI verifies that the checked-out zappMessaging SHA matches before building.
# Update when intentionally bumping a sibling dependency.

# The published SDK, whose history is squashed and so carries its own commit ids:
# this repository pins the mirror, not the development repo it is published from.
# GitHub: https://github.com/JustZappIt/zappmessaging-sdk
zappMessaging=a8b88ed4f6cc22382a4c79167340031aa12c42b1

# bare-kit is a direct clone of holepunchto/bare-kit v2.0.0 with no Zapp modifications.
# GitHub: https://github.com/holepunchto/bare-kit
# The local ../bare-kit/ directory has no git history; CI checks out the pinned commit.
# Update both this SHA and the workflow ref when upgrading bare-kit.
bare-kit=15a3569f3d704de7151761051c8d9cc2e299414f

# zcash-android-wallet-sdk is resolved from Maven snapshots, not includeBuild: upstream
# zodl ships SDK_INCLUDED_BUILD_PATH blank and requests ZCASH_SDK_VERSION from the
# central.sonatype.com snapshot repo, so we match it rather than building the Rust backend
# locally. This SHA is the provenance of that artifact, not a build input; CI does not
# verify it. v3.0.0 carries the ZODL Slipstream sync engine (enabled per-wallet via
# WalletCoordinator's isSlipstreamEnabled) and the OrchardMigrationSdk that drives the
# Orchard->Ironwood migration; v3.0.1 adds the Slipstream fixes upstream zodl 3.9.1 ships:
# the DB-backed chain-height fallback that stops transaction status flickering to Pending
# across a synchronizer rebuild, and a timestamp estimate for expired never-mined
# transactions. It also carries the semantic-types API break (Pczt, TransactionId).
# GitHub: https://github.com/zcash/zcash-android-wallet-sdk
zcashAndroidWalletSdk=b5a302cbbe6dd3da4a615dade221ca3461236304
